Vitruvian Courier (apps/desktop/vitruvian-courier): send the other person's read receipt when a
direct chat is synced and its latest message is mine and already read.

mautrix-gmessages only sends a read receipt when a live message update changes an outgoing
message's status to OUTGOING_DISPLAYED. A message read while the bridge was not watching (another
Google Messages web session held the connection, or the bridge was offline) therefore never gets
one, so Courier showed "Delivered" where Google Messages and Beeper show it was read. Conversation
syncs carry the latest message's status; this queues the receipt from it. Groups are left alone:
the conversation doesn't say who read it. Not fixed upstream as of v0.2610.0.

